[standards/application/api/STD-APP-API-000-developer-implementation-guide.md#812-rate-limiting-issues]

#### 8.1.2 Rate Limiting Issues

**Problem**: API returns 429 Too Many Requests

```json
{
    "error": "rate_limit_exceeded",
    "message": "Too many requests",
    "retryAfter": 60
}
```

**Solutions**:

1. **Implement exponential backoff**:

```javascript
async function apiCallWithRetry(url, options, maxRetries = 3) {
    for (let attempt = 0; attempt < maxRetries; attempt++) {
        try {
            const response = await fetch(url, options);

            if (response.status === 429) {
                const retryAfter = parseInt(response.headers.get('Retry-After')) || 1;
                const backoffDelay = Math.min(retryAfter * 1000, 2 ** attempt * 1000);

                console.log(`Rate limited. Retrying after ${backoffDelay}ms`);
                await new Promise((resolve) => setTimeout(resolve, backoffDelay));
                continue;
            }

            return response;
        } catch (error) {
            if (attempt === maxRetries - 1) throw error;
        }
    }
}
```

2. **Monitor rate limit headers**:

```javascript
const response = await fetch('/api/v1/users');
const remaining = response.headers.get('X-RateLimit-Remaining');
const reset = response.headers.get('X-RateLimit-Reset');

if (parseInt(remaining) < 10) {
    console.warn(`Rate limit nearly exhausted. Resets at: ${new Date(reset * 1000)}`);
}
```

